        "title": "Custom Skills can bind to a collaborating agent",
        "summary": "Skills now support delegating to a specific project agent, with server-side guards that keep cross-agent turns from being routed to stopped runtimes.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Skill creation and editing modals gained a new agent target field so authors can bind a custom Skill to a specific collaborating agent within the project, backed by end-to-end coverage for the skill-agent binding flow.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "edd5454149c261233187fedda5b6c3c504c1eeda"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a cross-agent runtime gate on the server: when a model tool triggers a delegation, Aura now checks the target agent's remote VM state and returns a tool-visible \"target agent is not available for delegation\" error unless the remote is running or working.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "edd5454149c261233187fedda5b6c3c504c1eeda"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Harness proxy create/update paths validate project membership, capability, and runtime availability when a Skill is pointed at a collaborating agent, with new integration tests covering the create and update flows.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "edd5454149c261233187fedda5b6c3c504c1eeda"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
